ests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the ADR 0059 §7 attribution: §7 (lines 518-544) does not state the whole-chain collapse-to-none premise — locate where that intent actually lives (the _intersect_capabilities docstring at runner_support.py:56-58 and rebar.toml:~190-193) and add the docstring to the 'stale documented intent' scope/AC, or cite the correct ADR section.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The whole-chain collapse-to-none is documented/approved intent — rebar.toml ~190-193, authorizing ticket 8fbd, and ADR 0059 §7 — resting on ONE premise: that a provider's cache keys \"would error on the candidate that does not share it\"'","ADR 0059 §7 (docs/adr/0059-...md:518-544) is titled 'Prompt caching is a capability, keyed per provider, with per-model floors' and discusses cache_settings_for keys, langchain#37042 shared-key rejection, and _MODEL_CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS floors — it contains no chain-wide capability-collapse/'would error on the candidate' reasoning","search of the ADR for 'intersect', 'collapse', 'would error' returns no matches within §7; the only fallback-chain capability-intersection mention is at line 479 in a different subsection ('What a consumer can infer')","The quoted 'would error on the candidate that does not share it' text is at src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py:56-58 (the _intersect_capabilities docstring), not in the ADR"],"finding":"The plan attributes the whole-chain 'collapse prompt_cache_style to none / mixed chain must fail closed because keys would error on the non-sharing candidate' PREMISE to ADR 0059 §7, but §7 (lines 518-544) does not contain that premise; it covers per-provider cache keys, the shared-automatic-key rejection, and per-model floors. The 'would error on the candidate that does not share it' rationale actually lives in the _intersect_capabilities docstring (runner_support.py:56-58).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f43dc9eaad9d63dae","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan — 'Prior art this reverses' section and Approach/Scope/AC referencing 'ADR 0059 §7'","norm_id":"n4a17dac8608e7ffa","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer opens ADR 0059 §7 to update the 'stale documented intent' per the AC and finds no collapse-to-none premise to supersede, leaving the actual source of the premise (the runner_support.py docstring at lines 56-58) unrevised.","Reviewer relying on the 'Prior art this reverses' argument cannot locate the §7 premise the reversal is predicated on."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Repoint the 'documented intent' references from 'ADR 0059 §7' to the _intersect_capabilities docstring (runner_support.py:56-58) plus rebar.toml:~190-193, and verify whether any ADR section actually needs a superseding note before committing to updating §7.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"